/**
@mainpage SGL User Manual

Simple Graphics Library (SGL) provides packed-image resize, crop and rotation,
RGB/YUV pixel-format conversion, and runtime services without using the C
standard library in the core implementation.

@section manual_start Start Here

- @ref getting_started explains configuration, linking, initialization, and
  shutdown.
- @ref image_operations describes resize, crop, rotate, and conversion calls.
- @ref pixel_formats defines byte layouts and buffer-size formulas.
- @ref runtime_services covers the memory pool, queue, and thread pool.
- The **Modules** and **Files** views contain the complete public API reference.

@section manual_contract Common Contract

- Include `<sgl-core.h>` for application-facing APIs.
- Image rows are tightly packed; public image functions do not accept stride.
- `SGL_RESTRICT` source and destination ranges must not overlap.
- The caller allocates all source and destination image buffers.
- Passing `SGL_NULL` as an image operation's pool selects single-thread
  execution.
- Initialize the global SGL memory pool before creating any LUT, queue, or
  thread pool, or before using an operation that requires temporary storage.

@section manual_build Build This Manual

From the repository root:

@code{.sh}
make docs
@endcode

The generated entry point is `build/<toolchain>/docs/html/index.html`. Doxygen
is an optional host dependency and is not required for a normal library build.

@section manual_release Release This Manual

Create self-contained, versioned documentation archives with:

@code{.sh}
make package-docs
@endcode

The `package/` directory receives `.tar.gz` and `.zip` archives plus a
`SHA256SUMS.txt` file. Each archive contains `html/index.html`, a release
README, and the project license. A generated manual is also installed under
`share/doc/sgl/html` by subsequent install and CPack operations.
*/
